27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[1,2,3,4,6,7,9,18,20,24,25,27,28,29,30,32]},{"id":"esau_1216","name":"Esau","also":"Edom, Edomite","summary":"Hairy, Rebekah’s first-born twin son (Gen. 25:25). The name of Edom, “red”, was also given to him from his conduct in connection with the red lentil “pottage” for which he sold his birthright (30, 31).","verses":151,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[3,4,6,8,11,13,17,18,19]},{"id":"laban_1803","name":"Laban","also":"","summary":"The son of Bethuel, who was the son of Nahor, Abraham’s brother. He lived at Haran in Mesopotamia. His sister Rebekah was Isaac’s wife (Gen. 24).","verses":46,"father":"Bethuel","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"abraham_58","name":"Abraham","also":"Abram","summary":"Father of a multitude, son of Terah, named (Gen. 11:27) before his older brothers Nahor and Haran, because he was the heir of the promises. Till the age of seventy, Abram sojourned among his kindred in his native country of Chaldea.","verses":277,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"isaac_616","name":"Isaac","also":"","summary":"The only son of Abraham by Sarah. He was the longest lived of the three patriarchs (Gen. 21:1-3).","verses":123,"father":"Abraham","mother":"Sarah","v":[9]}],"places":[{"id":"mahanaim_756","name":"Mahanaim","kind":"City","lat":32.21471,"lon":35.63291,"summary":"Two camps, a place near the Jabbok, beyond Jordan, where Jacob was met by the “angels of God,” and where he divided his retinue into “two hosts” on his return from Padan-aram (Gen. 32:2).","verses":13,"v":[2]},{"id":"edom_357","name":"Edom","kind":"Region","lat":31.25,"lon":34.75,"summary":"Idumea (Isa. 34:5, 6; Ezek. 35:15). “The field of Edom” (Gen. 32:3), “the land of Edom” (Gen. 36:16), was mountainous (Obad. 1:8, 9, 19, 21).","verses":79,"v":[3]},{"id":"seir_1042","name":"Seir","kind":"Region","lat":30.73469,"lon":35.60625,"summary":"The name of a mountainous region occupied by the Edomites, extending along the eastern side of the Arabah from the south-eastern extremity of the Dead Sea to near the Akabah, or the eastern branch of the Red Sea.","verses":24,"v":[3]},{"id":"jordan_653","name":"Jordan","kind":"Water (River)","lat":33.18645,"lon":35.61916,"summary":"But besides these two historical fountains there is a third, called the Hasbany, which rises in the bottom of a valley at the western base of Hermon, 12 miles north of Tell-el-Kady.","verses":177,"v":[10]},{"id":"jabbok_609","name":"Jabbok","kind":"Water (River)","lat":32.19324,"lon":35.6763,"summary":"A pouring out, or a wrestling, one of the streams on the east of Jordan, into which it falls about midway between the Sea of Galilee and the Dead Sea, or about 45 miles below the Sea of Galilee.","verses":7,"v":[22]},{"id":"peniel_930","name":"Peniel","kind":"","lat":32.18437,"lon":35.70287,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[30]},{"id":"penuel_931","name":"Penuel","kind":"City","lat":32.18437,"lon":35.70287,"summary":"Face of God, a place not far from Succoth, on the east of the Jordan and north of the river Jabbok. It is also called “Peniel.” Here Jacob wrestled (Gen. 32:24-32) “with a man” (“the angel”, Hos. 12:4.","verses":5,"v":[31]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3290,3290,1980,1870,1870,1870,4397,4397,4397,430,430,6293,0],[834,7200,7200,7200,3290,559,2088,4264,4264,4264,430,430,7121,7121,7121,1931,4725,4266],[3290,7971,4397,6440,6440,6440,413,251,251,6215,776,776,776,8165,8165,7704,7704,123,123],[6680,6680,6680,559,559,559,559,113,113,113,6215,5650,5650,3290,559,1481,1481,1481,1481,5973,3837,309,309,309,309,5704,6258],[1961,1961,7794,2543,6629,5650,8198,8198,7971,7971,7971,5046,5046,5046,5046,113,113,4672,4672,4672,4672,4672,2580,5869,5869,5869],[4397,4397,4397,7725,413,3290,559,559,935,935,413,